    "is_formula_typo": false,
    "reason": "The recursion was implemented exactly as SPEC/paper (eta_k = eta0 k^-0.501, projection, averaged iterate) and the warm-started average stays at theta* to ~1e-4, so the fixed point is correct. What makes the prescribed schedule slow is that the DI constraint leaves an effectively ill-conditioned problem: the population Hessian restricted to the constraint tangent space has smallest eigenvalue ~0.06, while the averaged-iterate transient decays like exp(-h * eta0 * k^(1-alpha)/(1-alpha)); with eta0=0.01 the transient factor at T=10^6 is still ~0.35, so ||theta_bar_T - theta*|| ~ 0.4-0.8 for T<=5e5. Reaching 1e-3 needs T ~ 10^9 at eta0=0.01 (or eta0 ~ 0.1 and T ~ 10^7). This is a step-size / problem-scale mismatch, not an algebra error."
  }
